\f0\fs24 \cf0 AWS Architecture Exercise\
---------------------------\
FixFast is a small appliance-repair company. It wants a simple website where customers can book a repair and upload a photo of the broken appliance. Staff use the same site to see and assign bookings. After each booking, the app sends the customer a confirmation SMS and email in the background, so the website never waits for them.\
The app has seven parts:\
A website (React)\
A backend API (Node.js)\
A database (PostgreSQL)\
Photo storage for uploaded images\
A message queue that holds jobs such as "send confirmation SMS"\
A background worker that picks jobs from the queue and sends the SMS and email\
User authentication: customers and staff log in with Google sign-in; staff and see admin screens only\
Your job: propose how to host and run this app on AWS, draw it, and explain it.\
\
What to explain: how the app will be built, run on AWS, from a user's request all the way to the database and back. For each area below, name the AWS service you would use, why you chose it, and how it connects to the rest of the app.\
Cover Basic Networking, Compute, Storage, Authentication, App Configuration and secrets, Monitoring, Deployment.\
\
What to Submit:\
One architecture diagram (draw.io or similar, with AWS icons)\
A short write-up (3\'965 pages or slides) Explaining the services and usecases}